<title>CANADA: Alberta issues 30 bln yen samurai bond at 5.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Alberta issues 30 bln yen samurai bond at 5.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>EDMONTON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian province of Alberta said it sold 30 billion yen or about US$268 million of three-year bonds in the Japanese samurai market to refinance a maturing U.S. dollar debt issue.</p>
<p>It said the refinancing was done at 5.2 percent in the retail market and swapped into floating rate U.S. dollars. This would save the province about 1/4 per cent a year in interest costs over the best alternative market, it said.</p>
<p>An earlier Reuters story from Tokyo said the bonds mature November 29, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
